## Gotchas learned
- Send ONE prompt at a time and wait for its report. Overlapping
  threads edited redis.ts at once and left two limiters behind.
- git grep skips untracked files: add --untracked.
- PowerShell treats [...path] as a wildcard: use -LiteralPath.
- git grep opens a pager: use git --no-pager, or press q.
- REDIS_KEY_PREFIX must NOT be in any local .env file.
- npm start runs with NODE_ENV=production; the key prefix does not
  depend on NODE_ENV, so local npm start still uses "dev:".

## WHEN DEPLOYING TO VERCEL
Set everything in Vercel > Project > Settings > Environment Variables,
never in a committed file.

1. Redis key prefix
   - Production: REDIS_KEY_PREFIX = prod:
     (nothing is deployed yet, so there are no old keys to keep;
     prod: avoids empty-value issues in the dashboard)
   - Preview: REDIS_KEY_PREFIX = preview:
   - Never leave it unset in Production, or prod shares "dev:" keys.
2. Spotify app
   - Production uses the CURRENT Spotify app (App A): its client id and
     secret go in Vercel, Production scope.
   - In the Spotify dashboard for App A, add the redirect URI
     https://<your-vercel-domain>/<same callback path as localhost>.
     Remove the localhost URI from App A.
   - Make sure her account is in App A's user list.
   - Create App B for dev: localhost redirect URI, both accounts in its
     user list, its id + secret in .env.local. Sign out and in again
     locally after switching.
3. Other env vars to copy into Vercel (Production): Upstash REST URL +
   token, DATABASE_URL, any NEXT_PUBLIC_* values (these are baked in at
   build time, so redeploy after changing them).
   Do NOT set SPOTIFY_LIVE in Vercel; it has no effect there.
   Optional: give dev its own Neon branch so mock-user rows never land
   in the production database.
4. Videos: don't ship large mp4s from public/ if avoidable; consider
   Vercel Blob or another host for them.
5. After the first deploy:
   - She signs in on the real domain and plays a song.
   - Mock badge is not visible; /api/spotify/diagnose returns 404.
   - Check Vercel logs for "[Rate Limiter]" lines; if they show up
